<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.c2a2.metabolism-regen</string>

    <!-- Rebuilds wiki/metabolism/metabolism_data.json from the live OpenStory db.
         Replaces the sandboxed metabolism-regen-daily task, which cannot finish:
         the 3GB db snapshot exceeds sandbox disk and its per-call time limit.
         Exit 3 = regen succeeded but ingest is stale (>48h) - a verdict, not a crash. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/env</string>
        <string>python3</string>
        <string>/Users/tomloughran/Documents/Claude/Projects/RC Karpathy Wiki Project/scripts/metabolism_monitor.py</string>
        <string>--regen-only</string>
    </array>

    <!-- Daily 06:00 local. Touches no git.

         WAS 05:00, moved 2026-10-26 to close the PRS triplet ordering race.
         The race, measured: new triplet .md files are written to disk by the
         sandboxed agent run (which cannot write .git), and the commit that
         publishes them is made by scheduled-commit-check at 05:45. prs_yield.py
         derives its series from a GIT HISTORY WALK and treats "on disk but not
         in history" as a hard Rule-12 failure ("the walk undercounted"). At
         05:00 that was true of every triplet produced since the previous day's
         commit, so the regen read a tree whose artifacts were half-published:
         2026-10-26 it exited 1 naming 42 such triplets (carroll/PRS-98..105,
         friston/PRS-82..84, hawkins/PRS-79..86, ...). The same script, same
         disk, re-run after the 05:45 commit landed exits 0 and dates all 42 to
         2026-10-26 - so the walk had not undercounted; history had not caught up.

         Of the two available orderings, this is the one that cannot create a
         half-written state. Committing EARLIER (before 05:00) would move the
         commit boundary toward the agent run that is still writing triplets,
         so a genuinely half-written triplet set could be committed and then
         believed by the yield series forever. Reading LATER only ever reads
         across a completed commit boundary; the worst case is staleness, not a
         corrupt history. 06:00 sits 15 min after scheduled-commit-check (which
         took 22s on 2026-10-26) and 30 min before Sunday 06:30
         metabolism-publish, whose freshness gate allows 36h.

         KNOWN CONSEQUENCE, not fixed here: the 05:45 health check now reports
         the PREVIOUS day's regen exit code, so a regen failure surfaces ~24h
         late. Fixing that means moving the health check after 06:00, or giving
         prs_yield.py a way to say "uncommitted in the working tree" instead of
         "absent from history" - both are Tom's call. -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>6</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/tomloughran/Documents/Claude/Projects/RC Karpathy Wiki Project</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/tomloughran/Library/Logs/c2a2-metabolism-regen.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/tomloughran/Library/Logs/c2a2-metabolism-regen.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
